# Worked examples and conformance

Each independent exchange starts with a fresh fixture namespace. The first two profiler exchanges are one job observed at two times. The remaining profiler exchanges are separate attempts. Repeated digits denote synthetic subjects, including illustrative release digests. The JSON block is an ordered list of exchanges; each has a caller request and the expected receipt. A published agent view consists of the operation description, expanded port types, rule meanings and the common status meanings from the [wire protocol](03-calls-and-receipts.md). A production catalog must resolve pinned types and show their constraints before selection.

## CPU · trimming

Choose run for ASCII space trimming. Supply text. The returned trimmed string may be empty. Wrong type rejects before executing; a crash rejects without a string.

```yaml
cc: "1"
id: text.trim
version: 1.0.0
carrier: fixture.invalid/text@sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
does: Remove leading and trailing ASCII spaces. An all-space input returns an empty string.
run: /tools/trim
takes: {text: string}
gives: {trimmed: string}
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"text": {"value": "  "}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "accepted","reason": "CHECKED","outputs": {"trimmed": {"value": ""}}}
  },
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"text": {"value": 3}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "rejected","reason": "INVALID_INPUT","outputs": {}}
  }
]
```

## Lab profiler · bounded attachment

Choose run for CPU stack samples, on the process identified by lease, PID and start ticks. Set seconds within 1–10. Reserve the target and authorize attachment before launch. A complete trace covers the window. A shortened trace is diagnostic. A missing sensor blocks admission and produces no trace. A lost detach acknowledgment yields unknown effects.

```yaml
cc: '1'
id: lab.sampler
version: 1.0.0
carrier: fixture.invalid/instrument@sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
does: Sample CPU stacks of one leased Linux process for 1â€“10 seconds. Attaching can perturb its
  timing. A short or interrupted capture is partial evidence.
run: /tools/sample
takes:
  target:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    required:
    - lease
    - pid
    - start_ticks
    properties:
      lease:
        type: string
        minLength: 1
      pid:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      start_ticks:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
  seconds:
    type: integer
    minimum: 1
    maximum: 10
gives:
  trace:
    artifact: application/x-ndjson
rules:
  inspect:
    kind: need
    meaning: Linux process inspector must verify lease, PID and process start ticks and grant scoped
      attach.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:process.inspect
      sha256: f59fc7fe46cbaee500b2f9e1d43b46457a3fe780ca451e70bd5b183ffc718805
  attach:
    kind: effect
    meaning: Attach sampler to the bound process and detach on stop. May perturb timing.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:process.attach
      sha256: 099d93ef02be9915f099a1e1cbdbb1253308ed564af6f0171d91ec7379441099
  coverage:
    kind: check
    meaning: Trace covers the requested duration and records sampling gaps.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:sample.coverage
      sha256: 02c3ffd8d2f56e188b733d820c1d3aba11184302c2cc04d354a1c79a022b56f6
needs:
- inspect
changes:
- attach
guarantees:
- coverage
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"target": {"value": {"lease": "lease.4","pid": 750,"start_ticks": 850}},"seconds": {"value": 5}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "running","reason": "STARTED","outputs": {},"job": "job.1"}
  },
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"target": {"value": {"lease": "lease.4","pid": 750,"start_ticks": 850}},"seconds": {"value": 5}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "rejected","reason": "PARTIAL_OUTPUT","outputs": {"trace": {"ref": {"uri": "fixture:three-seconds","sha256": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff"}}},"job": "job.1"}
  },
  {
    "request": {"key": "sampler-checked","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"target": {"value": {"lease": "lease.4","pid": 750,"start_ticks": 850}},"seconds": {"value": 5}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "accepted","reason": "CHECKED","outputs": {"trace": {"ref": {"uri": "fixture:full-trace","sha256": "0472f66e04930e7e0ffc7e9deab8b25d8fb4311e48df1a3897142ed324399015"}}},"job": "job.1"}
  },
  {
    "request": {"key": "sampler-missing_provider","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"target": {"value": {"lease": "lease.4","pid": 750,"start_ticks": 850}},"seconds": {"value": 5}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "blocked","reason": "MISSING_PROVIDER","outputs": {}}
  }
]
```

## Legacy bundle · inspect or measure

Inspect a native v3 pack with the read-only index provider and receive inventory after shard-bound checks. Measure instead sends the workload to the reserved loopback Strata endpoint and writes per-request observations to attempt storage. The source validators for these ports are only fixture locators. Native payload equivalence is unproven; publication is blocked until their pinned bytes and provider/effect definitions are supplied. The JSON below illustrates this bound failure, not a successful translation.

```yaml
cc: '1'
id: strata.lab-tools
version: 1.0.1
carrier: fixture.invalid/benchmark@sha256:9b083a97196866f7233e6e2948a46f4dc7fecb102dff2170d4e55a6ea8e8e30e
defs:
  workload:
    schema_ref:
      uri: fixture:workload-schema
      sha256: fe89e8f2a9770f7663c47b44b6ac32249804222ed45249b0fc1a4e2bdc5748e1
  pack:
    schema_ref:
      uri: fixture:pack-input
      sha256: 20df460932e0c4175e1d93bb043878fcdbed1618f05ea10277337806dc60a585
  observations:
    schema_ref:
      uri: fixture:observations-schema
      sha256: 710f025cbad41787fee9889cef2392b492cc282bbd99f10a8501de9face2c53d
  inventory:
    schema_ref:
      uri: fixture:inventory-output
      sha256: 659b0510e05be111c60ebb2eb494c6ef8e818aee1c303d70b379a1aad302f0b8
rules:
  strata-api:
    kind: need
    meaning: Loopback endpoint with agreed inference/status API on a reserved GB10 host. gb10. at
      least 1024 MiB
    definition:
      uri: fixture:strata-api
      sha256: 9e72726d0aa51888a6b0ecb0b294f15d52ae1c951b78473a8197652bfd52abad
  native-index:
    kind: need
    meaning: Read-only pinned Strata native pack and its declared shard layout. strata-native-index-v3.
      at least 128 MiB
    definition:
      uri: fixture:native-index
      sha256: b65dbf9aa5431ed454864d3ed42c4dd8dc8f95496e71e3efa83eeaa4fa562e93
  attempt.artifacts:
    kind: effect
    meaning: write raw per-request measurements
    definition:
      uri: fixture:attempt.artifacts
      sha256: 9f418b2b74543166ac4811bb868c3714e2c9108a49b77f6547ac100e201187f5
  output-schema:
    kind: check
    meaning: Check the raw per-request measurement schema.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:check-output-schema
      sha256: 1aa37b007787b293e80dfd79e6397a33dc2611ed8dc6e733d0c8065e6f94ef8a
  index-bounds:
    kind: check
    meaning: Check offsets and byte ranges against declared pack shards.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:native-index-bounds
      sha256: a58930157cfb8d6ded0b0061a07b163ce3851466264f63b7640c6925797da4bb
operations:
  measure:
    does: Collect per-request data with the pinned tools/dgx_bench.py wrapper
    run: /opt/cc/measure
    takes:
      workload: $workload
    gives:
      observations: $observations
    needs:
    - strata-api
    changes:
    - attempt.artifacts
    guarantees:
    - output-schema
  inspect:
    does: Inspect v3 native_experts.txt offsets and shard bounds for an upstream pack
    run: /opt/cc/inspect
    takes:
      pack: $pack
    gives:
      inventory: $inventory
    needs:
    - native-index
    changes: []
    guarantees:
    - index-bounds
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-inspect","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "inspect","inputs": {"pack": {"value": {"pack_id": "tiny"}}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "blocked","reason": "MISSING_PROVIDER","outputs": {}}
  },
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-measure","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "measure","inputs": {"workload": {"value": {"requests": 1}}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "blocked","reason": "MISSING_PROVIDER","outputs": {}}
  }
]
```

## Factory build · Strata header reader

The Factory builds the recipe once for the specified ABI. The caller supplies pack bytes to run and receives a format string. A damaged header yields TOOL_ERROR. A mutable base image or missing executable prevents release, before any caller can run it.

```yaml
cc: '1'
id: strata.header
version: 1.0.0
carrier:
  format: build-recipe
  source:
    repository: fixture:strata
    commit: '1111111111111111111111111111111111111111'
    tree: '2222222222222222222222222222222222222222'
  recipe:
    uri: fixture:reader-recipe
    sha256: a890b675cbe4ec768b37d50c36ff9eba9ee589b4b0d00dbfcc77d99c28abc6d8
  environment_lock:
    uri: fixture:arm64-lock
    sha256: 37d4b3f98b2da977b9d9c8f980a5d817f7f82404c57f46d177340838a1ff6f68
  target: linux/arm64
  build_context:
    uri: fixture:source-archive
    sha256: fe0b8b9a3222f27b20efc8b42971b00a3d55e224c3a64a2da2cef113299a418d
  base_image:
    format: oci-image
    image: fixture.invalid/instrument@sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
    platform: linux/arm64
does: Read the pack header and return the declared format; malformed headers fail.
run: /tools/header
takes:
  pack:
    artifact: application/octet-stream
gives:
  format: string
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"pack": {"ref": {"uri": "fixture:pack","sha256": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff"}}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "accepted","reason": "CHECKED","outputs": {"format": {"value": "v3"}}}
  }
]
```

## Strata/Muse · frozen measured subject

Bind the frozen subject manifest described in [Provenance](04-provenance.md). The GB10 and endpoint checks precede traffic. Read samples only after joining host and engine observations to the attempt. In this synthetic case the candidate uses more peak memory than its baseline. A checked capture therefore supports a negative evaluation. Missing required streams yield CHECK_UNAVAILABLE or PARTIAL_OUTPUT, depending on whether the checker or observation is missing.

```yaml
cc: '1'
id: muse.measure
version: 1.0.0
carrier: fixture.invalid/instrument@sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
does: Measure one frozen text-inference attempt. Return raw per-request timings and host samples
  for independent evaluation.
run: /tools/measure
takes:
  subject:
    artifact: application/vnd.ai4r.attempt+json
gives:
  samples:
    artifact: application/x-ndjson
rules:
  spark:
    kind: need
    meaning: Exclusive qualified GB10 lease and an endpoint attested to the input manifest.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:spark.lease
      sha256: 14a8c3b2fb6ed9d749c352d948cf2c71038cba7fbc04f8712eea462c2aee31f4
  traffic:
    kind: effect
    meaning: Issue inference requests to the leased endpoint within the admitted workload.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:endpoint.invoke
      sha256: 4afd7e4e4802eb97986c32a74bff8c12a550c1c8680f2ff1f943ee49e17f8f2b
  identity:
    kind: check
    meaning: Verify candidate restart identity, workload and required measurement streams.
    definition:
      uri: fixture:attempt.identity
      sha256: 8ef361bda3758478942e9b06e7b510e9c30945cc40264f0bb2df88747926a835
needs:
- spark
changes:
- traffic
guarantees:
- identity
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"subject": {"ref": {"uri": "fixture:frozen-muse-attempt","sha256": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff"}}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "accepted","reason": "CHECKED","outputs": {"samples": {"ref": {"uri": "fixture:request-and-host-samples","sha256": "9999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999"}}},"job": "job.1"}
  }
]
```

## Non-Strata · arithmetic

Choose run for integer addition. Supply a and b, read sum. Decimal inputs fail validation. No providers or effects are declared. This narrow arithmetic fixture exercises M2a call binding; the older calculation capsule has additional obligations listed below.

```yaml
cc: '1'
id: math.sum
version: 1.0.0
carrier: fixture.invalid/instrument@sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
does: Add two finite integers and return their sum.
run: /tools/add
takes:
  a: integer
  b: integer
gives:
  sum: integer
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "test-run","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "run","inputs": {"a": {"value": 2},"b": {"value": 3}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "call.1","attempt": 1,"status": "accepted","reason": "CHECKED","outputs": {"sum": {"value": 5}}}
  }
]
```

## Shared packet · report preview and external delivery

An agent can preview a research packet locally or deliver it to an authorized destination. Both operations accept the same packet. Only delivery can make a remote change. If the transport loses the acknowledgment, the runner retains the destination and idempotency key for reconciliation and forbids blind replay.

```yaml
cc: "1"
id: research.report
version: 1.0.0
carrier: fixture.invalid/report@sha256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
defs:
  packet: {type: object, required: [text], properties: {text: {type: string}}, additionalProperties: false}
rules:
  outbox:
    kind: need
    meaning: Authenticated delivery provider with a destination-scoped grant.
    definition: {uri: 'fixture:outbox', sha256: '0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef'}
  send:
    kind: effect
    meaning: Send the bound packet to the admitted destination once.
    definition: {uri: 'fixture:send', sha256: '0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef'}
operations:
  preview:
    does: Render packet text as Markdown for local review.
    run: /tools/preview
    takes: {packet: $packet}
    gives: {markdown: string}
  deliver:
    does: Submit packet text to the named destination and return its acknowledgment.
    run: /tools/deliver
    takes: {packet: $packet, destination: string}
    gives: {ack: string}
    needs: [outbox]
    changes: [send]
```

```json
[
  {
    "request": {"key": "preview-1","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "preview","inputs": {"packet": {"value": {"text": "Finding"}}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "preview.1","attempt": 1,"status": "accepted","reason": "CHECKED","outputs": {"markdown": {"value": "Finding"}}}
  },
  {
    "request": {"key": "deliver-1","release": "eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee","op": "deliver","inputs": {"packet": {"value": {"text": "Finding"}},"destination": {"value": "review.inbox"}}},
    "receipt": {"call": "deliver.1","attempt": 1,"status": "unknown","reason": "EFFECT_UNKNOWN","outputs": {}}
  }
]
```

## Twenty M2a inventory members

| Family and existing operations | Caller-visible behavior to preserve |
|---|---|
| Calculation · calculate, normalize_table | Validate typed columns, rounding and empty-table rules. Retain source and transformed packet. |
| Reporting · markdown_report, packet_report, summary_to_packet, deliver, deliver_paper | Local transforms and external delivery select separate effects. Uncertain publication requires outbox reconciliation. |
| Intent · compile_intent; contract · compile_requirements | Emit typed plans/requirements or missing-input evidence. An operation producing requirements cannot authorize them. |
| Literature · search, screen, rank, summarize_paper | Search binds a scoped provider. Preserve query/source pins and screening/ranking criteria. An empty result is valid. |
| Hypothesis · propose_hypothesis | A hypothesis with source references is a proposed claim, subject to later evaluation. Pin model/provider context; replay may only permit evidence inspection. |
| Build · build | Produces candidate source, recipe or image. Separate artifact integrity and independent qualification. |
| Evaluation · benchmark, evaluate | Separate observations from assessment. Freeze obligations, checkers and held-out evidence access before execution. |
| Planner · plan, plan_paper; generalist · run_on_jiuwenswarm | Return plans as data. Dynamic execution must bind child calls, scoped providers, effects and budgets before dispatch. Unbounded legacy behavior blocks migration. |

## Coverage of the source inventory

| Source family | Generation 1 representation and preservation test |
|---|---|
| M1 calculation, typed table normalization and Markdown reporting | Pure computation or typed transforms use JSON or artifact ports. Preserve table column/type obligations and report/reproduction artifacts. The math.sum example is smaller than the M2a calculation release. Dropping its report, reproduce, artifact.write grant or check IDs is an incompatible migration. |
| M1 generalist, discovery, screening and requirements | Prompts and rubrics are pinned implementation materials. Model/search access is scoped through needs and external calls through changes. Preserve source citations and headless missing-input behavior. If the generalist can dynamically invoke unconstrained tools, leave it unqualified until the adapter can enforce a ceiling. |
| M1 scientific evaluation, verifier, π benchmark | These operations return assessments or measurements. Preserve frozen checker/fixture identities, independence, access to held-out data and distinct outcome versus scientific verdict. A producer cannot assign itself acceptance authority. |
| M2a tool, skill, MCP, agent, workflow, data | Native interfaces can remain behind the process adapter. A workflow spawning children needs authorized bounded child calls, parent linkage and prebound budgets. A data package can expose a read-only lookup/export; a passive dataset remains an input artifact. An MCP adapter must retain remote failure and uncertain external-effect semantics. |
| Workshop 0.1 and 0.2, current 0.3 | Preserve original declaration and pinned materials. Earlier change request, patch/bundle/commit/image delivery and evaluation become companion records. A desired reader with unresolved ABI remains a draft. The two-operation diagnostic example retains the source port/check references, entrypoints and per-operation scope. Its synthetic predicates cannot qualify it. |
| Muse persistent Lab | Operate, inspect and adjust have distinct grants. A scoped adjust operation changes a private workspace and returns a patch/snapshot reference. Any subsequent scored run requires a frozen subject and confirmed restart. Restore or fork creates a fresh lease and attempt. |

## Rejecting and recovery fixtures

Apply each mutation independently to the named positive example. Reject at the first indicated boundary; never silently drop the offending field.

| Mutation | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| Repeat `id` in CPU YAML, or repeat an operation name in a bundle | Parser rejects duplicate key before a YAML library can overwrite it. |
| Supply both flat `run` and `operations`; type one port as both an artifact and an inline value | Reject conflicting declaration forms or ambiguous transport type. |
| Replace inspector input with `$absent`, or use its check ID as an effect | Reject unresolved or wrong-kind definition. |
| Add an unknown required profile | Reject at compile/admission. |
| Replace image digest with a tag; change recipe tree or supply a different ABI | Reject resolution/build with the corresponding compiler diagnostic. A well-formed pin still requires actual matching bytes. |
| Ask the diagnostic inspector for the benchmark write grant | Deny before launch. If an undeclared write is observed, record it and reject the receipt. |
| Ask for eleven profiler seconds; substitute a recycled PID; lose attach acknowledgment | Reject input, deny target admission, or return unknown effects respectively. Never automatically attach twice. |
| Replay an identical key; change its inputs; interrupt output persistence | Return existing job/receipt, return KEY_CONFLICT, or withhold acceptance until durable output is reconciled. |
| Declare an output as JSON string and return a number; remove a required checker result | Reject invalid output or withhold acceptance. A partial trace never satisfies a complete-coverage check. |

**Ownership review.** Package ID/version identify the release family. Carrier and entrypoint identify the executable. Description identifies the action, and output ports identify what callers can consume. Other author fields occur only when an example needs them. The compiler generates discovery summaries. The runner supplies immutable bindings, input-map references and uniform output checks. Duplicated identifiers required by M2a are generated from their owners.

**Source basis.** November 3 single-CC workshop 0.3 declaration, common carrier schema and qualified/draft examples; M2a 2.0.0-m2a.2 schema families and fixture corpus; M1 capsule extension release manifests and stage-role examples; reviewed 25-slide *Software Factory and Lab – Muse Spark addendum* (slides 2–6 for declaration/build, 16–17 for adjustment lineage, 18–25 for evidence and measurement). Source-reviewed Strata revision `c62d5e3a15b40ea51c96aae9e8d36928965f53ab`. These examples specify proposed behavior.


## Verification record · November 3

The focused notebook replay (Resources/tools/check_cc_protocol_examples.py) parsed seven authored declarations, expanded both CPU forms to the published JSON, validated thirteen synthetic M2a call/receipt projections, exercised rejection cases and checked the legacy diagnostic operation bindings. Three CPU process exchanges ran locally, including a valid empty string.

The existing workshop validator passed its linked records and nineteen rejecting cases. The older forms validator passed seven valid and eighteen rejecting cases. M2a passed its native eighteen fixtures across eight schemas. Eight M1 table-normalization fixture bodies ran directly against the original worker and checker, including malformed inputs and tampered output. The repository-wide pytest bootstrap requires additional dependencies. These results cover local contracts and fixture behavior. OCI builds, real profiler attachment, independent qualification and a GB10/Muse run remain unverified.

